\title{nightowl: Declarative Plots and Summary Tables with Inline Graphics for Clinical Research}
\description{
A small grammar for publication-ready statistical graphics built on 'ggplot2'. Plots are declared as layer stacks, optionally from 'YAML' style files, and rendered to 'SVG' with memoised rendering. Plots are first-class vector elements, so a column of a data frame can hold sparklines that render inside 'reactable' and 'kableExtra' tables. Includes an extensible summary table engine, colour-blind-safe palettes, a house theme, and helpers for snapshot-testing 'SVG' output.
